<div class="container my-5">

    <h1 class="text-center">Creating an Issue</h1>

    <p>
        Issues are the foundation of meaningful discussion.<br />
        They identify problems, gaps, or areas of uncertainty that can be explored, refined, and ultimately addressed.Creating an Issue
    </p>

    <p>Before creating a new issue, take a moment to consider how it fits within the broader knowledge graph:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Does this issue already exist in some form?</li>
        <li>Could it be a sub-issue of a larger topic?</li>
        <li>Or is it a meta-issue that connects multiple related problems?</li>
    </ul>


    <p>Clearly defining where your issue belongs helps keep the system organized and makes it easier for others to build on your work.</p>

    <p>Content submitted here should be a well-defined issue, not a general post or opinion. A strong issue is:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Specific and focused</li>
        <li>Clearly articulated</li>
        <li>Positioned within an existing context when possible</li>
    </ul>

    <p>All submissions go through a moderation process to ensure they meet quality standards. This helps maintain clarity, consistency, and usefulness across the platform.</p>
</div>